This covers the whole tree: the specification and the tour, the compiler,
the fixtures, the scripts, the site generator and the mark.  There are no
per-directory exceptions and no per-file headers; this file governs.

What `refine` produces is not a derivative work of `refine`.  Compiling a
program with this toolchain places no licensing condition on that program,
and neither does linking `core/*` into it.  What you compile is yours.

Third-party material carries its own notice next to it rather than here.
Today there is one: the icon paths in `assets/icons.py`, from Lucide, under
the ISC license, whose notice that file preserves.  Keep it.

Unless you state otherwise, a contribution you intentionally submit for
inclusion in this repository is licensed under the same dual terms, without
any additional conditions.
